# Development compatibility policy

nVyR is not a production or released product. Until the user explicitly changes
this policy, do not add backward-compatibility shims, legacy formats, version
fallbacks, or migration paths for previous development implementations.

Implement the current design directly. For example, a saved-file format change
does not need a compatibility flag to accommodate an older development ISO.

Preserve requested functionality, transaction safety, recovery, and per-image
isolation. These are current product requirements, not backward compatibility.
Do not expand a focused task into a repository-wide cleanup unless requested.
